{"kind":"deck","format":"deez.nut","version":2,"name":"CCAR-P Exam Prep — P0"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect define before selecting Claude architecture components?","The measurable business outcome, constraints, and success criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is “we need an AI agent” not a complete requirement?","It names an implementation preference rather than the underlying outcome and constraints."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which requirements should remain deterministic when correctness must not depend on probabilistic output?","Hard rules such as authorization, numeric thresholds, and schema validation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is a production Claude system more than a model call?","Because the request path also includes identity, context, tools, state, verification, outputs, observability, and recovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should be designed alongside the happy path?","The failure and recovery path."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should remain authoritative for current transactional facts?","The system of record, not chat history, a vector index, or a cached summary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What distinguishes a workflow from an agent in Anthropic's architecture guidance?","A workflow follows predefined code paths; an agent dynamically decides how to accomplish the task and use tools."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When is a workflow generally preferable to an agent?","When the process can be enumerated in advance and benefits from predictability and control."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When is an agent justified?","When required steps cannot be reliably predetermined and dynamic planning/tool use provides measured benefit."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the orchestrator-worker pattern?","A lead agent decomposes work, delegates bounded subtasks, and synthesizes worker results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What are strong reasons to use multiple agents?","Context isolation, parallel independent work, and meaningful specialization."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is prompt chaining?","A sequence where each stage consumes the previous stage's output."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is routing?","Classifying an input and sending it to the appropriate specialized path."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is model-token cost alone insufficient for architecture comparison?","Total solution cost also includes engineering, infrastructure, human review, monitoring, incidents, and compliance overhead."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What must exist before claiming a business improvement?","A baseline and measurable outcome."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Outcome requirement","The measurable value or change the solution should create."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Risk constraint","A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["System of record","The authoritative source for current operational state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Idempotent retry","A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Workflow","LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Agent","A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Orchestrator","The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Context isolation","Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization","Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Routing","Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Technical metric","A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Business metric","An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Architecture should begin with the {{c1::business outcome}}, not the preferred AI component.","D1.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Hard authorization rules belong in {{c1::deterministic controls}} rather than relying only on prompts.","D1.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Convert vague goals into {{c1::measurable targets}} before choosing a model or pattern.","D1.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For stateful workflows, define {{c1::state ownership}} explicitly rather than treating model context as durable state.","D1.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Design the {{c1::failure path}} at the same time as the happy path.","D1.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Current transactional facts should come from the {{c1::system of record}}.","D1.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A {{c1::workflow}} follows predefined paths, while an agent dynamically chooses its process.","D1.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Prefer the {{c1::least autonomous}} pattern that still meets the requirement.","D1.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Multi-agent systems are justified by meaningful {{c1::isolation, parallelism, or specialization}}, not by novelty.","D1.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["The orchestrator should verify {{c1::coverage and worker outputs}} before synthesis.","D1.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Use {{c1::parallelization}} only when subtasks are genuinely independent.","D1.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["An {{c1::evaluator-optimizer}} loop needs measurable evaluation criteria, not vague critique.","D1.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Before claiming improvement, define a measurable {{c1::baseline}}.","D1.6"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Compare architectures using {{c1::total solution cost}}, not model-token cost alone.","D1.6"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What requirement category includes latency, availability, residency, throughput, and cost constraints?","Non-functional requirements"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What implementation request should be treated as a hypothesis rather than a requirement when a stakeholder asks for one?","Agent"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes the authoritative source for current operational state?","System of record"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What property allows a side effect to be safely retried without unintended duplication?","Idempotency"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What pattern uses predefined LLM/tool code paths?","Workflow"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What pattern lets the model dynamically choose steps and tool use?","Agent"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What multi-agent pattern uses a lead agent to delegate bounded subtasks?","Orchestrator-workers"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes keeping worker contexts separate to reduce interference?","Context isolation"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What decomposition pattern classifies a request and sends it to a specialized path?","Routing"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes the starting measurement used to quantify improvement?","Baseline"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A stakeholder says, “Build us an autonomous agent.” What should the architect do first?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome, constraints, and measurable success criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the most capable Claude model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Create a multi-agent architecture.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Implement MCP for every backend.\"}]","a","Architecture starts from the outcome and constraints; “agent” is an implementation hypothesis."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A finance workflow must classify expenses but refunds over $500 require exact enforcement. Where should the $500 rule live?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"In deterministic policy/authorization logic outside the model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"In a few-shot example.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only in the model's explanation.\"}]","a","Hard thresholds should not depend on probabilistic model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team has not defined what “better customer support” means. What is the best architecture next step?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define measurable outcome and acceptance criteria before selecting components.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add retrieval immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Benchmark the largest model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Start with an autonomous agent and refine later.\"}]","a","A solution cannot be evaluated without a measurable target."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which requirement should most strongly constrain architecture before model selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A rule that regulated decisions require human approval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A preference for a fashionable framework.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A desire to use as many tools as possible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A preference for longer prompts.\"}]","a","Risk constraints can rule out otherwise capable architectures."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A task is exact schema validation after Claude generates JSON. What is the strongest design?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Validate the schema deterministically after generation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Tell Claude to be extra careful.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a second model only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add more examples but no validator.\"}]","a","Exact invariants are best enforced by deterministic software."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let Claude issue the credit directly if the prompt says to be cautious.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Store account balance in conversation memory.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry the credit call automatically after any timeout without idempotency.\"}]","a","Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Whether the prompt is long enough.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Whether the model is the largest available.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Whether the response was friendly.\"}]","a","Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A vector index contains yesterday's account balance. The user asks for the current balance. What should supply the answer?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The authoritative account system/API.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The vector index because retrieval is faster.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A cached summary from yesterday.\"}]","a","Current operational state should come from the system of record."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A multi-step agent fails intermittently, but no component shares a trace identifier. What architecture capability is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"End-to-end observability/correlation across the request path.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More worker agents.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More verbose system prompts.\"}]","a","The system must be reconstructable across components."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A deterministic workflow.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fully autonomous agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent swarm.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An open-ended planner with unrestricted tools.\"}]","a","The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A bounded agent with dynamic planning.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fixed one-step prompt only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A rigid workflow with every path enumerated.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A schema validator alone.\"}]","a","Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["One model call plus retrieval reliably solves a bounded classification task. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep the simple augmented-LLM design unless evaluation shows a need for more orchestration.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents for resilience.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add an evaluator loop by default.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Split every label into a separate agent.\"}]","a","Complexity should earn measurable value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A system needs flexible investigation but exact approval before money moves. Which architecture is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A hybrid: bounded agent for investigation plus deterministic approval/execution gates.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fully autonomous agent with a warning prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A fixed workflow that cannot adapt to evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only a human with no automation.\"}]","a","Hybrid designs place flexibility where useful and deterministic controls at consequential boundaries."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One shared mutable prompt for all workers.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A worker agent for every sentence.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A fixed sequential chain even though tasks are independent.\"}]","a","Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add more workers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove tracing to reduce overhead.\"}]","a","Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A single agent with two tools already completes a task reliably. What is the strongest reason NOT to add three specialist agents?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The extra coordination complexity has no demonstrated benefit.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Agents cannot call tools.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelism is never useful.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Subagents cannot have separate context.\"}]","a","Multi-agent complexity should be justified by isolation, parallelism, or specialization."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An orchestrator assumes every worker completed its assigned section and publishes an incomplete report. What control is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Coverage/completeness validation before synthesis.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger font in the final report.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More token budget for the orchestrator only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Removing worker boundaries.\"}]","a","The coordinator must verify required work, not merely concatenate outputs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Prompt chaining with validation between stages.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Unbounded multi-agent exploration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallel execution of all stages.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No decomposition because multiple calls are always bad.\"}]","a","Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Independent searches across four jurisdictions are required. Which pattern best reduces wall-clock time?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize the independent searches and combine results.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Run them sequentially by default.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Route all four to one identical result.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use evaluator-optimizer without parallel work.\"}]","a","Independent work can be parallelized safely."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Requests belong to billing, technical support, or sales, each with different tools. Which pattern best fits?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Routing to specialized paths.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One giant prompt with every tool.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluator-optimizer only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A random worker selection.\"}]","a","Classification followed by specialized handling is the routing pattern."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A generated report can be scored against a precise rubric and revised until it passes. Which pattern fits?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluator-optimizer.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Routing.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Simple parallelization.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Unconditional retries.\"}]","a","The evaluator provides criterion-based feedback to an optimizer/generator."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always choose the cheaper model call.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always choose the higher-capability model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore human-review cost because it is not AI spend.\"}]","a","Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team reports 95% model accuracy but cannot say whether customer resolution time improved. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A link between technical performance and a business outcome/baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More agent autonomy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second vector database.\"}]","a","Technical metrics must connect to value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which measurement best supports an ROI claim for an automation project?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Change from a pre-defined baseline in a business-relevant outcome, including ongoing costs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Number of prompts written.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Total tokens consumed.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Number of tools exposed.\"}]","a","ROI requires baseline, outcome, and cost."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A complex multi-agent design is 1% more accurate but doubles latency and operational burden. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate whether the measurable business gain justifies the added total cost and SLA impact.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose multi-agent because accuracy is always dominant.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore operational burden.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove evaluation and decide by architecture sophistication.\"}]","a","Architecture trade-offs must be justified by business value and constraints."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support translating business problems into Claude-based solutions?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Select the strongest model before clarifying the workload.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use prompt wording as the only authorization control.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.; Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing translating business problems into Claude-based solutions. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat the word “agent” as a mandatory architecture requirement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Skip measurable targets until after launch.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.; Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in translating business problems into Claude-based solutions?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use prompt wording as the only authorization control.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define success and failure criteria before implementation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume every step should use an LLM.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.; Define success and failure criteria before implementation.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define success and failure criteria before implementation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Skip measurable targets until after launch.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Treat stakeholder implementation preferences as hypotheses.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Select the strongest model before clarifying the workload.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define success and failure criteria before implementation.; Treat stakeholder implementation preferences as hypotheses.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support end-to-end Claude architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat vector retrieval as the source of truth for current transactions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume chat history is durable application state.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.; Keep durable application state outside model context.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing end-to-end Claude architecture. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retry every failed side effect blindly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Design only the happy path.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep durable application state outside model context.; Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in end-to-end Claude architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume chat history is durable application state.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Make failures visible to operators.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Let each worker keep conflicting copies of critical state.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.; Make failures visible to operators.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on end-to-end Claude architecture, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Make failures visible to operators.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Design only the happy path.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use the authoritative source for live transactional state.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat vector retrieval as the source of truth for current transactions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Make failures visible to operators.; Use the authoritative source for live transactional state.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use a workflow when steps are predictable.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an agent whenever a task has more than one step.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents before testing a single-agent design.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use a workflow when steps are predictable.; Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume tool use automatically makes a system an agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat autonomy as inherently better.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.; Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents before testing a single-agent design.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use hybrids to combine flexible reasoning with deterministic gates.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore repeated-inference latency and cost.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.; Use hybrids to combine flexible reasoning with deterministic gates.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use hybrids to combine flexible reasoning with deterministic gates.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat autonomy as inherently better.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluate complexity against latency, cost, and reliability.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use an agent whenever a task has more than one step.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use hybrids to combine flexible reasoning with deterministic gates.; Evaluate complexity against latency, cost, and reliability.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support multi-agent orchestration?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Create one agent per trivial step.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume worker completion without validation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.; Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing multi-agent orchestration. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Share mutable critical state without ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across workers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Lose trace continuity at handoffs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.; Propagate trace identity across workers.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in multi-agent orchestration?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across workers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume worker completion without validation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign state ownership deliberately.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use multi-agent architecture when one agent already meets requirements.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Propagate trace identity across workers.; Assign state ownership deliberately.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on multi-agent orchestration, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Assign state ownership deliberately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Lose trace continuity at handoffs.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate coverage before synthesizing.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create one agent per trivial step.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Assign state ownership deliberately.; Validate coverage before synthesizing.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support decomposing complex problems?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Decompose when stages need different context or tools.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Split work by organizational chart instead of information boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate useful intermediate outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM for every deterministic transformation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Decompose when stages need different context or tools.; Validate useful intermediate outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing decomposing complex problems. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Validate useful intermediate outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Pass entire worker transcripts when concise outputs suffice.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelize only independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add critique loops with no measurable rubric.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Validate useful intermediate outputs.; Parallelize only independent work.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in decomposing complex problems?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize only independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM for every deterministic transformation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep deterministic transforms in code when appropriate.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Parallelize steps with hidden dependencies.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Parallelize only independent work.; Keep deterministic transforms in code when appropriate.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on decomposing complex problems, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep deterministic transforms in code when appropriate.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add critique loops with no measurable rubric.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Avoid decomposition when coordination cost exceeds benefit.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Split work by organizational chart instead of information boundary.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep deterministic transforms in code when appropriate.; Avoid decomposition when coordination cost exceeds benefit.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support aligning architecture to business value?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define a baseline before claiming improvement.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize token cost even when task success drops.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat human review as free.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define a baseline before claiming improvement.; Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing aligning architecture to business value. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Report model accuracy without business context.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Include human review and operational complexity in cost.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore operations and compliance cost.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.; Include human review and operational complexity in cost.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in aligning architecture to business value?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Include human review and operational complexity in cost.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat human review as free.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluate SLA effects alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Prefer sophistication over measurable value.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Include human review and operational complexity in cost.; Evaluate SLA effects alongside quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on aligning architecture to business value, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate SLA effects alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore operations and compliance cost.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Measure cost per successful outcome.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Optimize token cost even when task success drops.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate SLA effects alongside quality.; Measure cost per successful outcome.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a sound discovery-to-architecture flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the business outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Quantify success and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Separate model vs deterministic responsibilities\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the simplest viable architecture\"}]","The architecture follows the outcome and constraints, not the reverse."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a typical protected request path.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the caller\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate input and gather context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run model/tool work\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply deterministic verification\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute output/action and record telemetry\"}]","Identity and validation precede model/tool work; protected execution follows verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a sensible architecture-escalation strategy.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Test a simple augmented model call\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Add a workflow if predictable stages are needed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Use a bounded agent if dynamic planning is required\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Add multi-agent complexity only when evaluation justifies it\"}]","Start simple and escalate only when measured requirements demand it."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order the orchestrator-worker pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Interpret the overall goal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Decompose into bounded subtasks\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Delegate work to workers\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Collect and validate results\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Synthesize the final result\"}]","The orchestrator plans, delegates, validates, then synthesizes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a prompt-chaining workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Run the first bounded stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate its intermediate output\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Pass the validated result to the next stage\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Produce and verify the final output\"}]","Dependent stages execute in order with validation at useful boundaries."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a routing workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Receive the request\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Classify the request type\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Select the specialized path/tools\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Execute that path and return the result\"}]","Routing first identifies the category, then chooses the corresponding path."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a simple value chain for an AI architecture.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish the baseline\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Measure the technical improvement\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Observe the operational change\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Measure the business outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Compare against ongoing total cost\"}]","Value is established by comparing measurable outcome changes and ongoing cost to the baseline."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should drive Claude model selection?","Measured workload requirements across quality, latency, cost, tool use, context needs, and risk."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why should model names not be hard-coded as permanent architecture assumptions?","Model lineups have lifecycle states and change over time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should happen after changing the model in production?","Re-run workload-specific regression, latency, safety, and cost evaluations."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the role of a system prompt in architecture?","To provide trusted behavioral instructions, scope, constraints, and output expectations."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is a system prompt not an authorization boundary?","Model compliance is probabilistic; protected actions need enforceable controls outside the model."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["How should untrusted retrieved/user content be handled relative to trusted instructions?","Keep it structurally separated and do not allow it to silently redefine policy."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When should few-shot examples be added?","When representative examples measurably improve ambiguous behavior, formatting, tone, or boundary cases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is zero-shot prompting?","Giving clear task instructions without examples."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the key principle of context engineering?","Put the smallest useful set of high-signal information in the model's active context for the current decision."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is more context not automatically better?","Irrelevant or stale context consumes tokens and can compete with relevant information."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What content is a strong candidate for prompt reuse/caching?","Large stable instructions or reference material reused across many requests."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What content is a poor caching candidate?","Frequently changing transactional state that must be current."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active model","A fully supported model recommended for current use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Deprecated model","A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Behavioral instruction","Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Enforceable control","Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Zero-shot","Clear direct instructions without worked examples."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Few-shot / multishot","Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active context","Information currently visible to the model for the present inference."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Compaction","Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Prompt template","Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
